Two more Codex P2s, both on the cancellation path added in 46fef69, and both
valid. The premise I had wrong: I assumed nothing persists during a drag, so
cancelling in memory was enough. handleProjectMutation calls persistWorkspace,
so a deletion mid-drag writes the PREVIEWED order to storage.

1. Cancel now persists what it restored. Without it a reload resurrects the
   abandoned arrangement even though memory looked correct.
2. Cancel now drops panes it empties. The subtle part: handleProjectMutation
   installs a fallback tab for a pane it would empty, but it counts the dragged
   tab that is previewing into that pane, so it installs nothing. Taking the
   tab back out on cancel then strands a blank pane. Falls back to a home tab
   if every pane would be empty, matching closeTab's guard.

Both regression tests confirmed to fail without their fix: the persist one
reloads to ["Settings","New work"], the empty-pane one leaves 2 panes.

Test trap worth remembering: a seeded tab title does NOT survive decorateTab.
A project tab seeded as "Doomed" renders as "Project", so selecting by
data-workspace-tab-title silently matches nothing and the test times out on
boundingBox. Select by data-workspace-tab-id instead - that attribute was added
in a19089e for the drag geometry and doubles as a stable test hook.

